","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-23T15:04:41Z","updated_at":"2025-01-23T15:13:57Z","body":"Would be good to get a call stack from that to see what calls the decoding\n\nThere are a few places where `get_id_path` without calling `has_id` first, I suspect they are the place it happens","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2610054316/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2610092019","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2610092019","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2610092019,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bktfz","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-23T15:18:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-23T15:18:49Z","body":"I can't reproduce it now (╯°□°)╯︵ ┻━┻\n\nI debugged it before, but forgot to grab the exact stack trace. It was somewhere here:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b0655dc86f096b3496a9ab5b18965676d4fb35ba/modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_extend_parser.cpp#L209-L214\n`scr_path` was `uid://`, which translates to 0, which translates to `uid://a`. The script has this line:\n```GDScript\nif path.begins_with(\"uid://\"):\n```\nwhich might've wrongly caused the error. But it seems random.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2610092019/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2610103845","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2610103845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2610103845,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bkwYl","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-23T15:23:29Z","updated_at":"2025-01-23T15:23:29Z","body":"I think it'd be reasonable to add `has_id` in necessary places, where the path can't be ensured, and handle things gracefully\n\nProbably some different underlying issue though causing it to push a broken value somehow","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2610103845/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613757499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2613757499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2613757499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bysY7","user":{"login":"anknetau","id":3803433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDM0MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3803433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau","html_url":"https://github.com/anknetau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T03:35:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T03:35:49Z","body":"I am really struggling to reproduce this one on my M1, will try Intel Windows 10 shortly","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613757499/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677394221","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2677394221","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2677394221,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6flcst","user":{"login":"theraot","id":1212509,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTI1MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1212509?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot","html_url":"https://github.com/theraot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T04:07:41Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T04:07:41Z","body":"I just ran into this in Godot 4.4.rc1. In my project it happened when saving any of two specific scripts in an external editor. To figure out if the problem was the UIDs of the scripts or the contents, I removed most of the code of one of them (everything except the `class_name` line), and the error went away. Then comparing the code between the two scripts let me to the culprit: the code contains the string `\"uid://\"`.\n\nSearching in the reproduction project I find something similar: The file `InstanceSlot.gd` contains the line `if path.begins_with(\"uid://\"):`. Thus I believe this is the same issue and a new one with the same symptom.\n\nAnd for what is going on, I believe the system is trying to parse that `\"uid://\"` to give us a clickable link to jump to the resource. Which fails with the error message `ERROR: Unrecognized UID: \"uid://a\".` on the editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677394221/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2752834282","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2752834282","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2752834282,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kFOrq","user":{"login":"mattmag","id":3790261,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3OTAyNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3790261?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag","html_url":"https://github.com/mattmag","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattmag/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T00:32:20Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T00:38:19Z","body":"Had this occur v4.4 stable x64 Windows 11.\n\nI don't have a debug version built, but running with --verbose shows this:\n\n`ERROR: Unrecognized UID: \"uid://a\".\n   at: (core/io/resource_uid.cpp:170)`\n\nUpdate: The error happens on project load if VS code is open before I open godot, otherwise, it doesn't happen until I double click a script file to launch the external editor.\n\n`[LSP] Connection Taken` precedes the error in the Godot Output window each time.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2752834282/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753973203","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2753973203","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2753973203,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kJkvT","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T10:42:43Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T11:04:32Z","body":"I got this error after deleting some resource files in the editor. So the necessary cleanup was not done when deleting resource files in the editor.\n\nFor file deletion from outside the editor, it may be necessary to provide functionality to clean up invalid uids.\n\nA pop-up window pops up when such errors are received, prompting the user to check and clean up to avoid outputting these errors every time the project is reopened.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Create a scene and save it,\n2. Set the scene as the main scene,\n3. Delete the scene and then reopen the project.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753973203/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2762897319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2762897319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2762897319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6krnen","user":{"login":"LeifintheWind","id":114954877,"node_id":"U_kgDOBtoSfQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114954877?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind","html_url":"https://github.com/LeifintheWind","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeifintheWind/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-29T00:03:01Z","updated_at":"2025-03-29T00:05:06Z","body":"I get this error when my script has the line\n\n`newFilePath.contains(\"uid://\")`\n\nWhen the file is saved the error is produced. When I comment out that line it no longer produces the error.\n\nSeems like a script containing `\"uid://\"` gets engine to think that this is supposed to be a \"valid uid\" that it should read and cache or something.\n\nYup, just tested it with `var temp = \"uid://\"` and it produces the same error.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2762897319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790556703","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2790556703","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2790556703,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mVIQf","user":{"login":"axv3658","id":8991121,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTExMjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8991121?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658","html_url":"https://github.com/axv3658","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/axv3658/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T18:12:44Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T18:16:07Z","body":"Not a fix but a workaround that was successful in my project:\n1. close your project + editor\n2. make a copy of the `.godot` folder in the project root directory\n3. delete the `.godot` folder in the project root directory\n4. restart your project + editor\n\nNote that this will also reset the editor's save state (open scripts and scenes, selected scene in the inspector, etc will all be cleared)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790556703/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800026340","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2800026340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2800026340,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m5QLk","user":{"login":"straightupgruntled","id":60860773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwODYwNzcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60860773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled","html_url":"https://github.com/straightupgruntled","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T16:41:49Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T16:41:49Z","body":"I had this issue occur with a project, and I discovered something maybe useful. It turned out the left over references for me were things that had to do with the Project Settings config. My project settings had lost reference to my icon after cleaning up UID and resource import files outside of the Godot Engine. I simply went into the settings and reset these, and the errors went away.\n\nMaybe there should be some way for the engine to check if there are any project settings referencing reimported assets, especially when regenerating the UIDs.\n\nThe broken references for my and my project were the game icon, and the cursor sprite. Simply resetting these fixed the issues for me.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800026340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800027137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2800027137","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2800027137,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m5QYB","user":{"login":"straightupgruntled","id":60860773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwODYwNzcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60860773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled","html_url":"https://github.com/straightupgruntled","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/straightupgruntled/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T16:44:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T16:44:10Z","body":"> I got this error after deleting some resource files in the editor. So the necessary cleanup was not done when deleting resource files in the editor.\n> \n> For file deletion from outside the editor, it may be necessary to provide functionality to clean up invalid uids.\n> \n> A pop-up window pops up when such errors are received, prompting the user to check and clean up to avoid outputting these errors every time the project is reopened.\n> \n> Steps to reproduce:\n> \n>     1. Create a scene and save it,\n> \n>     2. Set the scene as the main scene,\n> \n>     3. Delete the scene and then reopen the project.\n\nThis leads me to think it has to do with project settings related references being broken, and resetting them fixes the solution.\n\nI was able to figure this out by going into the project file in Notepad++ and search for the UID strings that were causing me issues, and was able to figure out which project settings referenced that UID string.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800027137/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800067803","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2800067803","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2800067803,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m5aTb","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T18:31:23Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T18:31:23Z","body":"This issue is specifically about `uid://a`.\nUnrecognized UID is a common error. It may happen if you try to refer to a deleted file.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800067803/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2935944226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2935944226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2935944226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u_vQi","user":{"login":"shomykohai","id":61943525,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTQzNTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61943525?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai","html_url":"https://github.com/shomykohai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shomykohai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T15:23:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T15:23:05Z","body":"This happens in [my addon](https://github.com/shomykohai/quest-system/blob/main/addons/quest_system/plugin.gd#L17-L35) too.\nI can confirm that it happens only if VSCode takes the LSP connections, and keeps being spammed if I edit plugin.gd from there.\n\n```\n[LSP] Connection Taken\n  ERROR: Unrecognized UID: \"uid://a\".\n  ERROR: Unrecognized UID: \"uid://a\".\n  ERROR: Unrecognized UID: \"uid://a\".\n```\n\nI'm not sure if the issue comes from Godot directly, or from the extension [godot-tools](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-vscode-plugin).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2935944226/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2962414172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-2962414172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":2962414172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wktpc","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T12:02:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T12:02:53Z","body":"We're able to reproduce this 100% with this simple MRP: [lsp-uid-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20689460/lsp-uid-mrp.zip)\n\nThe repro steps are as simple as:\n1. Open the project in VS Code, with the [godot-tools](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=geequlim.godot-tools) extension running.\n2. Open `main.gd` in VS Code.\n3. Open the project in the editor.\n4. Connect the godot-tools extension to the editor, if it hasn't done so itself.\n\nThat'll produce the following output:\n```\n[LSP] Connection Taken\nERROR: Unrecognized UID: \"uid://a\".\nERROR: Unrecognized UID: \"uid://a\".\n```\n\nRestarting the editor and reconnecting the LSP client will produce the error again.\n\nAs mentioned here already it's because the LSP server is trying to parse the GDScript files for any clickable links by running every string literal through `FileAccess::file_exists` as part of `ExtendGDScriptParser::update_document_links`. More specifically, we end up with this call stack (on Linux):\n\n```\nResourceUID::get_id_path(const ResourceUID * this, ResourceUID::ID p_id) (core/io/resource_uid.cpp:199)\nResourceUID::uid_to_path(const String & p_uid) (core/io/resource_uid.cpp:211)\nFileAccess::fix_path(const FileAccess * this, const String & p_path) (core/io/file_access.cpp:261)\nFileAccessUnix::file_exists(FileAccessUnix * this, const String & p_path) (drivers/unix/file_access_unix.cpp:315)\nExtendGDScriptParser::update_document_links(ExtendGDScriptParser * this, const String & p_code) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_extend_parser.cpp:214)\nExtendGDScriptParser::parse(ExtendGDScriptParser * this, const String & p_code, const String & p_path) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_extend_parser.cpp:1054)\nGDScriptWorkspace::parse_script(GDScriptWorkspace * this, const String & p_path, const String & p_content) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_workspace.cpp:428)\nGDScriptWorkspace::reload_all_workspace_scripts(GDScriptWorkspace * this) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_workspace.cpp:220)\nGDScriptWorkspace::initialize(GDScriptWorkspace * this) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_workspace.cpp:401)\nGDScriptLanguageProtocol::initialize(GDScriptLanguageProtocol * this, const Dictionary & p_params) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_language_protocol.cpp:205)\ncall_with_variant_args_ret_helper<GDScriptLanguageProtocol, Dictionary, Dictionary const&, 0ul>(GDScriptLanguageProtocol * p_instance, Dictionary (GDScriptLanguageProtocol::*)(GDScriptLanguageProtocol * const, const Dictionary &) p_method, const Variant ** p_args, Variant & r_ret, Callable::CallError & r_error) (core/variant/binder_common.h:672)\ncall_with_variant_args_ret<GDScriptLanguageProtocol, Dictionary, Dictionary const&>(GDScriptLanguageProtocol * p_instance, Dictionary (GDScriptLanguageProtocol::*)(GDScriptLanguageProtocol * const, const Dictionary &) p_method, const Variant ** p_args, int p_argcount, Variant & r_ret, Callable::CallError & r_error) (core/variant/binder_common.h:715)\nCallableCustomMethodPointer<GDScriptLanguageProtocol, Dictionary, Dictionary const&>::call(const CallableCustomMethodPointer<GDScriptLanguageProtocol, Dictionary, Dictionary const&> * this, const Variant ** p_arguments, int p_argcount, Variant & r_return_value, Callable::CallError & r_call_error) (core/object/callable_method_pointer.h:105)\nCallable::callp(const Callable * this, const Variant ** p_arguments, int p_argcount, Variant & r_return_value, Callable::CallError & r_call_error) (core/variant/callable.cpp:57)\nCallable::callv(const Callable * this, const Array & p_arguments) (core/variant/callable.cpp:84)\nJSONRPC::process_action(JSONRPC * this, const Variant & p_action, bool p_process_arr_elements) (modules/jsonrpc/jsonrpc.cpp:128)\nJSONRPC::process_string(JSONRPC * this, const String & p_input) (modules/jsonrpc/jsonrpc.cpp:172)\nGDScriptLanguageProtocol::process_message(GDScriptLanguageProtocol * this, const String & p_text) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_language_protocol.cpp:141)\nGDScriptLanguageProtocol::LSPeer::handle_data(GDScriptLanguageProtocol::LSPeer * this) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_language_protocol.cpp:96)\nGDScriptLanguageProtocol::poll(GDScriptLanguageProtocol * this, int p_limit_usec) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_language_protocol.cpp:250)\nGDScriptLanguageServer::_notification(GDScriptLanguageServer * this, int p_what) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_language_server.cpp:62)\nGDScriptLanguageServer::_notification_forwardv(GDScriptLanguageServer * this, int p_notification) (modules/gdscript/language_server/gdscript_language_server.h:38)\nObject::_notification_forward(Object * this, int p_notification) (core/object/object.cpp:931)\nObject::notification(Object * this, int p_notification, bool p_reversed) (core/object/object.h:889)\nSceneTree::_process_group(SceneTree * this, SceneTree::ProcessGroup * p_group, bool p_physics) (scene/main/scene_tree.cpp:1183)\nSceneTree::_process(SceneTree * this, bool p_physics) (scene/main/scene_tree.cpp:1263)\nSceneTree::process(SceneTree * this, double p_time) (scene/main/scene_tree.cpp:695)\nMain::iteration() (main/main.cpp:4756)\nOS_LinuxBSD::run(OS_LinuxBSD * this) (platform/linuxbsd/os_linuxbsd.cpp:979)\nmain(int argc, char ** argv) (platform/linuxbsd/godot_linuxbsd.cpp:85)\n```\n\nIt would seem to me that `FileAccess::fix_path` is the problem here, since you can't really fix/resolve a non-existent UID, no matter how well-formatted it is, and it currently has no way of reporting such a failure to its caller.\n\nI've thrown together a quick-and-dirty fix/hack here: #107402","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2962414172/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3219380215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-3219380215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101962","id":3219380215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_49f3","user":{"login":"olivatooo","id":15200079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjAwMDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15200079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo","html_url":"https://github.com/olivatooo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivatooo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-25T08:47:33Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T08:47:33Z","body":"Is there a way to completely disable UIDs in godot? This just generates more problems and does not solve anything","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3219380215/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3219510903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101962#issuecomment-3219510903","